commit e3e82f98cb905831b0f1508f6352382d32daa364
Date: Tue Sep 15 01:01:13 2026 -0700

rpc-budget: never cache a null answer; commit: held batch no longer blocks

Root cause of the receipt timeouts: eth_getTransactionReceipt is hash-addressed
so the response cache kept its first answer forever, including null from a
lagging node. Every poll for the whole 240s deadline was served that null,
and the morning's hold-and-recheck then re-polled it for 30 minutes, cutting
commits to one batch per ~35 min. A null is no longer cached, and a held
batch excludes its reports from the next one instead of blocking it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


